# --- pass 5: bodies --------------------------------------------------------------------
# The tokens are taken in segments that end at a page end or at a string: the nodes and args
# of a segment go to small windows over the tables (5 and 3 pages) that are copied back after
# it, and a text literal's bytes, which have no bound, are decoded into args between segments.
# byte p1 of a text literal segment: state (two-page args window, pairs decoded, esc); the
# pair (3 v) of a byte that is not a backslash is operand p5 + k of the half (k the pairs so
# far, p5 wrapping below 0 before the half), written at pair (p5 + k - p6) of the window
# (p6 the half's pair at window word 0) when it is within the half
fn txtb (u32x128x2,u32,u32) u32 u32x128 u32x128 u32 u32 u32 -> (u32x128x2,u32,u32)
w at p0 0
k at p0 1
esc at p0 2
q add p4 p1
qh shr q 7
ql and q 127
isl eq qh 0
cl get p2 ql
ch get p3 ql
c select isl cl ch
isbs eq c 92
e1 eq esc 1
isn eq c 110
ist eq c 116
m0 select isn 10 c
m1 select ist 9 m0
v select e1 m1 c
skip select e1 false isbs
pr add p5 k
pin lt pr 16384
put select skip false pin
wr sub pr p6
f mul wr 2
h0 shr f 7
l0 and f 127
g0 get w h0
o0 get g0 l0
v0 select put 3 o0
g0b set g0 l0 v0
w1 set w h0 g0b
