 h187 h188 h189 h190 h191 h192 h193 h194 h195 h196 h197 h198 h199 h200 h201 h202 h203 h204 h205 h206 h207 h208 h209 h210 h211 h212 h213 h214 h215 h216 h217 h218 h219 h220 h221 h222 h223 h224 h225 h226 h227 h228 h229 h230 h231 h232 h233 h234 h235 h236 h237 h238 h239 h240 h241 h242 h243 h244 h245 h246 h247 h248 h249 h250 h251 h252 h253 h254 h255
ret r
end
# the operand table of the bodies, given the first half p0 and the operand count p1 from the
# run of pass 5 from 0 and that run's inputs p2..p10: the second half is a second run when
# there are more than 16384 operands
fn bodyargs u32x128x256 u32 u32x128x45 u32x128x64 u32x512x64 u32x128x384 u32x128x128 u32x128x128 u32 u32 u32 -> u32x128x512
big gt p1 16384
c select big 1 0
z call z256
hi fold p5hi c z p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10
r call argcat p0 hi
ret r
end
# --- capacities -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The front end's tables hold 131072 source bytes (lex.a0 `readsrc`), 16384 tokens of at most
# 32767 bytes, 8192 symbols, 51200 pool bytes, 4096 uses, 820 functions, 2730 nodes, 32768
# operands, and 8320 types and tlist words; the checker adds at most one type per node, so
# the parser's types plus the nodes must fit 8320. A source beyond one of them is the limit
# diagnostic 4 (tools/bootstrap.ts `planChunks` cuts programs so that every chunk fits).
# the longest token of page p1 so far (p0)
fn toklen u32 u32 u32x128x3 -> u32
w0 mul p1 3
w2 add w0 2
h shr w2 7
l and w2 127
g get p2 h
v get g l
b gt v p0
r select b v p0
ret r
end
fn toklpg u32 u32 u32x128x384 u32 -> u32
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
g3 mul p1 3
ga get p2 g3
g31 add g3 1
gb get p2 g31
g32 add g3 2
gc get p2 g32
grp arr ga gb gc
r fold toklen cnt p0 grp
ret r
end
# over a capacity: tokens p0 (p1 of them), symbols p2, pool bytes p3, uses p4, functions p5,
# types p6, tlist p7, nodes p8, operands p9
fn fecap u32x128x384 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 u32 -> bool
t0 gt p1 16384
tc select t0 16384 p1
n127 add tc 127
np shr n127 7
ml fold toklpg np 0 p0 tc
t1 gt ml 32767
s0 gt p2 8192
o0 gt p3 51200
u0 gt p4 4096
f0 gt p5 820
ty add p6 p8
y0 gt ty 8320
l0 gt p7 8320
d0 gt p8 2730
a0 gt p9 32768
b0 or t0 t1
b1 or b0 s0
b2 or b1 o0
b3 or b2 u0
b4 or b3 f0
b5 or b4 y0
b6 or b5 l0
b7 or b6 d0
r or b7 a0
ret r
end
# --- writers: page p1 of a table holding p3 words ------------------------------------------
fn wstep384 io u32 u32x384 -> io
v get p2 p1
w write p0 v
ret w
end
fn wty io u32 u32x384x65 u32 -> io
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 384
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 384
cnt select big 384 rest
w fold wstep384 cnt p0 pg
ret w
end
fn w16 io u32 u32x128x16 u32 -> io
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
w fold wword cnt p0 pg
ret w
end
fn w32 io u32 u32x128x32 u32 -> io
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
w fold wword cnt p0 pg
ret w
end
fn w45 io u32 u32x128x45 u32 -> io
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
w fold wword cnt p0 pg
ret w
end
fn w65 io u32 u32x128x65 u32 -> io
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
w fold wword cnt p0 pg
ret w
end
fn w128 io u32 u32x128x128 u32 -> io
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
w fold wword cnt p0 pg
ret w
end
fn w400 io u32 u32x128x400 u32 -> io
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
w fold wword cnt p0 pg
ret w
end
fn w512 io u32 u32x128x512 u32 -> io
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
w fold wword cnt p0 pg
ret w
end
# the sym table from the symbol ranges: (pool start, len) with the starts summed in order
fn wsymst (io,u32) u32 u32x128 -> (io,u32)
tk at p0 0
ps at p0 1
v get p2 p1
len and v 32767
w1 write tk ps
w2 write w1 len
ps2 add ps len
r rec w2 ps2
ret r
end
fn wsympg (io,u32) u32 u32x128x64 u32 -> (io,u32)
pg get p2 p1
base mul p1 128
rest sub p3 base
big gt rest 128
cnt select big 128 rest
r fold wsymst cnt p0 pg
ret r
end
# io front: read n then n source bytes; write code, token index, then each table preceded by
# its word count (all zero on an error). The result is the error code.
fn parseio io -> u32
rs call readsrc p0
src at rs 0
n at rs 1
t1 at rs 2
lx call lexsrc src n
toks at lx 0
nw at lx 1
ntok div nw 3
s1 call pass1 src toks ntok
sinfo at s1 1
ta at s1 2
tv at s1 3
uses at s1 4
hdrs at s1 5
nsym at s1 7
nuses at s1 8
umode at s1 10
uerr at s1 11
uetok at s1 12
nhdr at s1 15
uopen ne umode 0
uerr0 eq uerr 0
ueof and uerr0 uopen
e1 select ueof 1 uerr
et1 select ueof ntok uetok
s2 call pass2 src sinfo nsym
pool at s2 0
npool at s2 1
s3 call pass3 src toks ta hdrs nhdr e1 et1 ntok
types at s3 0
tlist at s3 2
hout at s3 4
ntypes at s3 5
ntlist at s3 6
e3 at s3 11
et3 at s3 12
nhc at s3 18
nhn at s3 19
s4 call pass4 hout nhn nhc
fns0 at s4 0
names at s4 1
derr at s4 2
dtok at s4 3
dup ne derr 0
e4 select dup derr e3
et4 select dup dtok et3
s5 call pass5 fns0 names src toks ta tv ntok e4 et4 0
fns at s5 0
nodes at s5 1
alo at s5 2
narg at s5 5
args call bodyargs alo narg fns0 names src toks ta tv ntok e4 et4
nnodes at s5 4
nargs at s5 5
fcs at s1 7
fcu at s1 8
fcp at s2 1
fch at s3 19
fct at s3 5
fcl at s3 6
fcn at s5 4
ovr call fecap toks ntok fcs fcp fcu fch fct fcl fcn narg
code0 at s5 8
code select ovr 4 code0
etok at s5 9
ok eq code 0
w0 write t1 code
w1 write w0 etok
npoolw select ok npool 0
nsymw0 mul nsym 2
nsymw select ok nsymw0 0
nsymc select ok nsym 0
ntypesw0 mul ntypes 3
ntypesw select ok ntypesw0 0
ntlistw select ok ntlist 0
nfnsw0 mul nhc 7
nfnsw select ok nfnsw0 0
nnodesw0 mul nnodes 6
nnodesw select ok nnodesw0 0
nargsw0 mul nargs 2
nargsw select ok nargsw0 0
nusesw select ok nuses 0
w2 write w1 npoolw
pp127 add npoolw 127
ppn shr pp127 7
w3 fold w400 ppn w2 pool npoolw
w4 write w3 nsymw
sy127 add nsymc 127
syn shr sy127 7
ws0 rec w4 0
ws fold wsympg syn ws0 sinfo nsymc
w5 at ws 0
w6 write w5 ntypesw
ty383 add ntypesw 383
tyn div ty383 384
w7 fold wty tyn w6 types ntypesw
w8 write w7 ntlistw
tl127 add ntlistw 127
tln shr tl127 7
w9 fold w65 tln w8 tlist ntlistw
w10 write w9 nfnsw
fn127 add nfnsw 127
fnn shr fn127 7
w11 fold w45 fnn w10 fns nfnsw
w12 write w11 nnodesw
nd127 add nnodesw 127
ndn shr nd127 7
w13 fold w128 ndn w12 nodes nnodesw
w14 write w13 nargsw
ar127 add nargsw 127
arn shr ar127 7
w15 fold w512 arn w14 args nargsw
w16 write w15 nusesw
us127 add nusesw 127
usn shr us127 7
w17 fold w32 usn w16 uses nusesw
ret code
end
